{"reference":"Psalms 113","book":"Psalms","chapter":113,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Surrounding Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"A disputed contextual reading places the psalms that follow within a larger collection that preserves memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile, while also gathering thanksgiving for return, festival praise, meditation on Torah, and Songs of Ascents oriented toward worship. This provides a broader setting for reading Psalms 114–118 alongside Psalm 113.","verse_refs":["Psalms 114:1-8","Psalms 115:1-18","Psalms 116:1-19","Psalms 117:1-2","Psalms 118:1-29"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_113_b86d1ce5a9cb910cffca4edc"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}